.TH  1 "2026-08-05" "rakudo (2024.09)" "User Contributed Raku Documentation"




.SH "NAME"

onefite \- Create, fit, plot, convert, archive, and serve OneFit\-Engine models
.SH "SYNOPSIS"


.RS 4m
.EX
onefite [\-h|\-\-help]
onefite [\-v|\-\-version]
onefite man [\-m|\-\-man]

onefite create FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]
onefite fit FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]
onefite fit INPUT\-FILE [OPTIONS]
onefite random FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]
onefite plot INPUT\-FILE [OPTIONS]

onefite list [models|aliases] [\-\-quiet]
onefite help MODEL [KEY] [\-\-quiet]
onefite convert INPUT\-FILE OUTPUT\-FILE [\-\-work\-folder=DIR]

onefite archive [\-\-fit=ENTRY] [EXTRA\-OPTION \&.\&.\&.]
onefite ar      [\-\-fit=ENTRY] [EXTRA\-OPTION \&.\&.\&.]
onefite log     [\-\-fit=ENTRY] [EXTRA\-OPTION \&.\&.\&.]
onefite path [PATH\-OPTION \&.\&.\&.]

onefite service start [OPTIONS]
onefite service stop
onefite service log
onefite service PID
onefite start\-web\-engine [OPTIONS]
onefite stop\-web\-engine

onefite test list
onefite test [TEST \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]
onefite upgrade [OPTIONS]
onefite uninstall

.EE
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.P
onefite is both the command\-line interface and a small HTTP micro\-service for OneFit\-Engine (OFE)\&. It imports experimental data, creates engine descriptions, compiles user\-defined model functions, performs individual, global, or hybrid/mixed nonlinear least\-squares fits using CERNLIB MINUIT, produces plots (via Grace/xmgrace, as PDF, optionally animated to MPEG4), and optionally archives or packages the results\&.

A fit can be started from a model expression and one or more data files:

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b)=a+b*x' data\&.dat

.EE
.RE
.P
It can also be started from an existing OneFit\-Engine \&.json or \&.sav description:

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit experiment\&.json

.EE
.RE
.P
Unless another directory is selected, temporary fit files are written beneath the current directory\&. Informational messages are normally written to standard error; command results are written to standard output\&. Successful fits can optionally be recorded to a local archive/log for later lookup (see archive/ar/log below)\&.
.SH "COMMANDS"

.SS create

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite create FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]

.EE
.RE
.P
Parse a model expression and its data files, compile the generated model code, and emit or save an OFE description \fIwithout running a fit\fR\&. If \-\-save\-to is omitted, the generated JSON is written to standard output\&. create is the only command that understands \-\-ist\-ffc\-Mz; it has no \-\-no\-plot, \-\-archive, \-\-zip\-to, or fit\-quality options (\-\-hybrid, \-\-mp4, \-\-print\-cols, \-\-R2, \-\-reduced\-chi2, \-\-error\-bars, \-\-parallel, \-\-workers, \-\-remove\-outliers, \-\-ramdisk) since no fit is actually performed\&.
.SS fit

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]
onefite fit INPUT\-FILE [OPTIONS]

.EE
.RE
.P
Run a fit from either a model expression or an existing \&.json/\&.sav engine file\&. Most options below are shared between the two forms \- see "COMMON OPTIONS" for exactly which ones apply to which form\&.

The expression form imports the supplied data, resolves model aliases, compiles generated code, runs the selected MINUIT methods, and optionally saves, archives, or packages the result\&. If the expression contains a parameter declaration ending in \&.MIXED=1, global mode is turned on automatically (this automatic detection applies only to the expression form, not to the input\-file form below)\&.

The input\-file form reloads an existing engine description; it understands \-\-export and \-\-individual, which the expression form does not, but does \fInot\fR understand the data\-import options (\-\-data\-label, \-\-gfilt, \-\-fit\-if, \-\-plot\-if, \-\-range, \-\-R1, \-\-set\-err, \-\-SymbSize, \-\-sef\-R1\-file, \-\-tags, \-\-aux\-code) since the definition already has them baked in\&. By default, it also creates a ZIP archive whose name is derived from INPUT\-FILE\&. Use \-\-zip\-to to select another archive name\&.
.SS random

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite random FUNCTION [DATA\-FILE \&.\&.\&.] [OPTIONS]

.EE
.RE
.P
Assign random initial values within each bounded parameter range, mark those parameters fixed, and run the resulting model\&. random has no \-\-fit\-methods, \-\-aux\-code, \-\-archive, or #\-prefixed dynamic override support, and its "skip plotting" flag is spelled \-\-inp/ \-\-no\-plot rather than the \-np/\-\-no\-plot used by fit\&.
.SS plot

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite plot INPUT\-FILE [OPTIONS]

.EE
.RE
.P
Render plots from an existing \&.json or \&.sav file without fitting\&. The command creates a work directory named after INPUT\-FILE and packages the plot results\&. plot only understands the auto\-scale/log\-scale flags, \-\-Num/\-\-npts, and \-\-work\-folder \- it has no \-\-quiet, \-\-save\-to, or any fit\-quality option\&.
.SS convert

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite convert INPUT\-FILE OUTPUT\-FILE [\-\-wf|\-\-work\-folder=DIR]

.EE
.RE
.P
Convert between OneFit\-Engine \&.json files and fitteia \&.sav files (direction is inferred from the two file extensions given)\&. The default working directory is /tmp\&.
.SS list

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite list [\-\-quiet]
onefite list models [\-\-quiet]
onefite list aliases [\-\-quiet]

.EE
.RE
.P
With no selector, print both installed model metadata and aliases\&. models prints C/META\-C\&.json\&. aliases merges the installed aliases\&.json with a local \&./aliases\&.json; local entries take precedence\&.
.SS help

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite help MODEL [\-\-quiet]
onefite help MODEL KEY [\-\-quiet]

.EE
.RE
.P
Print all metadata for MODEL, or only the value associated with KEY\&. If MODEL is not found the command still exits successfully and reports a "not found" message instead\&.
.SS archive, ar, and log

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite archive
onefite archive \-\-fit=ENTRY [EXTRA\-OPTION \&.\&.\&.]

.EE
.RE
.P
archive, ar, and log are three names for the same command\&. Without \-\-fit, they print the fit history: one 0\-indexed line per entry (index, timestamp, archive filename and size, and the original command)\&. With \-\-fit=ENTRY, they unzip that entry's archived data and re\-run the exact original command against it\&. ENTRY may be that printed index, or last\-N to count back N entries from the most recent; any other value (including the literal word last) falls back to the most recent entry\&. Any additional, otherwise\-unrecognised named option is appended verbatim to the re\-run command, which lets you replay a stored fit with extra flags applied:

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite archive \-\-fit=last
onefite ar \-f last\-1 \-\-rchi2
onefite log \-f 2 \-\-ro=1

.EE
.RE
.SS path

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite path [\-s|\-\-src] [\-t] [\-\-exa|\-\-examples] [\-b|\-\-bin] [\-l|\-\-lib]
             [\-c|\-C] [\-\-log] [\-a|\-\-aliases] [\-\-ar|\-\-archive]

.EE
.RE
.P
Print installed paths\&. With no selector, print all known paths\&.
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-s, \-\-src \- OneFit\-Engine source directory\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-t \- Raku test directory (\fIt/\fR)\&. Short option only; there is no \-\-t long form\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-exa, \-\-examples \- Examples directory\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-b, \-\-bin \- Installed executable directory\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-l, \-\-lib \- Raku/C library directory (holds the compiled C/Fortran static libs)\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-c, \-C \- C and Fortran source directory\&. Both are short options; there is no \-\-C long form\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-log \- Log directory (holds the running service's log file)\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-a, \-\-aliases \- Configuration directory containing installed aliases\&.json\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ar, \-\-archive \- Fit archive\-log directory\&.
.RE

Examples

.RS 4m
.EX
cd $(onefite path \-s)
vi $(onefite path \-a)/aliases\&.json
cat $(onefite path \-\-log)/onefite

.EE
.RE
.SS service

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite service start [\-\-ip=ADDRESS] [\-p|\-\-port=PORT] [\-d|\-\-systemd\-daemon]
                      [\-\-rd|\-\-ram|\-\-ramdisk|\-\-RAMDisk|\-\-use\-ramdisk]
onefite service stop
onefite service log
onefite service PID

.EE
.RE
.P
Start or manage the OFE HTTP service\&. The default bind address is 0\&.0\&.0\&.0 and the default port is 8142\&. Bind to 127\&.0\&.0\&.1 when the service should only be reachable from the local machine (see SECURITY below)\&.

\-\-systemd\-daemon reloads systemd, enables onefite\&.service, and starts the service\&. Without it, the service is started in the background (from $HOME/public_html) by killing any already\-running instance and relaunching start\-web\-engine under nohup\&. \-\-use\-ramdisk copies $HOME/public_html onto a fresh RAM disk (backing the original up to $HOME/public_html_bak first) before starting the service\&.

service log shows the service log file; service PID prints its process id (found via ps aux | grep start\-web\-engine)\&.
.SS start\-web\-engine and stop\-web\-engine

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite start\-web\-engine [\-\-ip[=ADDRESS]] [\-p|\-\-port[=PORT]]
onefite stop\-web\-engine
(OBSOLETE) onefite start\-engine [\-\-np|\-\-no\-plot] [\-q|\-\-quiet] [\-\-wf|\-\-work\-folder=DIR]

.EE
.RE
.P
Run the HTTP engine directly, in the foreground \- what service start/ stop ultimately drive\&. If \-\-ip is omitted it is auto\-detected from the machine's first IPv4 address (falling back to 127\&.0\&.0\&.1)\&. See "HTTP API" below for the routes it serves\&. stop\-web\-engine stops the process matching start\-web\-engine\&.

start\-engine is an older, obsolete alternative: instead of an HTTP server it watches the current directory for \&.sav/\&.json files (optionally prefixed __fit__/__plot__/__fit\-only__ to pick the action) and fits/plots each as it appears, in an infinite loop\&. Prefer the HTTP service or the plain fit/plot commands instead\&.
.SS HTTP API

start\-web\-engine (and therefore service start) serves a small Cro\-based HTTP application on \-\-ip:\-\-port\&. Every request is appended to the service log together with the requesting host and, for /fit and /convert, the time taken\&.
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
GET / \- a minimal HTML upload form (useful for smoke\-testing the service from a browser); it posts to /fit or /convert\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
GET/POST /list, /list/models, /list/aliases \- text/plain output identical to onefite list [models|aliases] \-\-quiet\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
GET/POST /help/MODEL[/KEY] \- text/plain output identical to onefite help MODEL [KEY] \-\-quiet\&. The POST form takes multipart fields model (required) and, optionally, one further field whose \fIvalue\fR is used as KEY (any field name works; only its value is inspected)\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
GET/POST /man \- text/plain body containing the troff/groff rendering of this manual (what Pod::To::Man produces), not plain text\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
POST /fit \- multipart upload\&. Required field file (a \&.dat/ \&.txt/\&.zip/\&.hdf5/\&.\&.\&. data file)\&. All other fields are optional and mirror the fit FUNCTION \&.\&.\&. command\-line options under the same short or long names, including function, fit\-methods/fm, Num/npts, SymbSize/ssz, global/g, hybrid/mixed, mpeg4/mp4, autox/autoy/autoxy, logx/logy/logxy (and their aliases), reduced\-chi2/rchi2, R1, R2/pearson\-correlation, sef\-R1\-file, print\-cols, err/set\-err, range, remove\-outliers, fit\-if, plot\-if, gfilt, username (per\-user work folder), and any #\&.\&.\&.\-prefixed field for a dynamic parameter override\&. Boolean\-style fields are truthy on "yes" or 1\&. A download field selects the response: "zip" streams back the whole work folder as a zip (application/octet\-stream); "json" streams back the saved fit definition (FOLDER/BASENAME\&.json, where FOLDER and BASENAME derive from the uploaded file's own name); any other non\-empty value is treated as a path relative to that same per\-upload folder and streamed back verbatim; when download is absent, the response is the text/plain fit log instead\&. The temporary per\-request work folder is deleted once the response has been sent\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
POST /convert \- multipart upload, required field file (a \&.sav or \&.json file)\&. Converts it to the other format and streams the result back as application/octet\-stream\&.
.RE
.SS test

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite test list
onefite test [TEST \&.\&.\&.] [\-\-verbose|\-v] [\-d|\-\-systemd\-daemon] [\-p|\-\-post\-install]

.EE
.RE
.P
test list lists the available \&.rakutest files by name, without running them\&. test with no file arguments runs the full suite via prove6 \-\-lib t/; given one or more TEST names (with or without the \&.rakutest suffix), only those are run and their combined output is captured and printed\&. Systemd\-daemon and post\-install checks are enabled by default; disable them with \-\-no\-systemd\-daemon/\-\-no\-post\-install when inappropriate for the current platform\&. \-\-post\-install always fits a small built\-in dataset via the plain command line and checks the result\&. If \-\-systemd\-daemon is set and systemctl status onefite reports it active, it also fits the same dataset by curl\-ing the running HTTP service on 127\&.0\&.0\&.1:8142; otherwise, if a background service process is found (onefite service PID), it curls that instead; if neither is running, the HTTP check is skipped with a note that the service is off, and only the command\-line check runs\&.
.SS upgrade

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite upgrade [\-u|\-\-to\-user] [\-c|\-\-compile] [\-d|\-\-systemd\-daemon]
                [\-\-cernlib] [\-\-shell] [\-\-shell\-port=PORT]
                [\-\-ip=ADDRESS] [\-p|\-\-port=PORT] [\-\-test]
                [\-m|\-\-merge\-site=BRANCH] [\-\-minuit=COUNT]
                [\-\-wsl|\-\-macos|\-\-docker] [\-\-apt|\-\-apt\-get|\-\-dpkg] [\-\-git]

.EE
.RE
.P
Update the current checkout (git stash && git pull, unless \-\-no\-git) and invoke INSTALL with the corresponding options, then restart the service\&. \-\-minuit defaults to whatever the currently\-built MINUIT already supports (read back from its own compiled\-in \fId506cm\&.inc\fR) rather than a fixed number\&. Git update, compilation, and package update are enabled by default\&. Boolean options can be negated with \-\-no\-NAME or \-\-/NAME\&.
.SS uninstall

Stop the web engine, update the source checkout, and run INSTALL \-U\&. This removes the installed OneFit\-Engine components and may require elevated privileges\&.
.SH "MODEL"
EXPRESSIONS

A model expression has this general form:

.RS 4m
.EX
OUTPUT[OUTPUT\-RANGE](X[X\-RANGE], PARAMETER, \&.\&.\&.) = EXPRESSION

.EE
.RE
.P
Parameters may be written as follows:
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a \- free parameter with engine\-selected initialization
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a:1\&.0 \- free parameter initialized to 1\&.0
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a[0<10]  \- free parameter bounded to the inclusive range 0 through 10
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a:1\&.0[0<10]  \- initialized and bounded parameter
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a=1\&.0 \- fixed parameter
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a=1\&.0[0<10]  \- fixed parameter that still carries an allowed range
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
a=1\&.0[0<10]\&.MIXED=1  \- per\-block parameter in a \-\-hybrid fit (see FITTING MODES)
.RE

Both '<'  and ';' are accepted as range separators, though '<'  usually requires less escaping inside a quoted shell argument\&.

A backslash before + marks separately\-plotted model contributions:

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b,c)=a\+b*x+c*x*x' data\&.dat

.EE
.RE
.P
Quote the complete expression to prevent the shell from interpreting spaces, '<' , #, *, parentheses, or backslashes\&.
.SH "ALIASES"


Installed aliases are read from the installation aliases\&.json\&. A local \&./aliases\&.json is merged over the installed file, with local entries taking precedence\&. Aliases can be selected in several equivalent forms:

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'alias: one exponential' data\&.dat
onefite fit 'a: one exponential' data\&.dat
onefite fit '#one\-exponential' data\&.dat

.EE
.RE
.P
Use \-\-define\-alias=NAME (\-a/\-\-da/\-\-dali; also \-\-alias on the expression form of fit) after fitting to create or replace a local alias with the fitted function\&.
.SH "FITTING"
MODES
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
Individual \- fit each data set independently\&. This is the default unless the engine file or command selects another mode; \-i/\-\-individual forces this mode, and is only available when loading an existing engine file (fit INPUT\-FILE)\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
Global \- \-g/\-\-global minimizes a shared objective across all supplied data sets\&. Available on create, random, and both forms of fit\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
Hybrid or MIXED \- \-\-hybrid enables mixed fitting and also implies global mode\&. It is only available on fit (either form); create and random do not support it\&. A function expression containing a \&.MIXED=1 parameter declaration automatically activates global mode too, but only when fitting from a function expression directly (fit FUNCTION \&.\&.\&.), not when re\-fitting a saved INPUT\-FILE\&. Parameters tagged \&.MIXED=1 are fitted per data set while the remaining (untagged) parameters participate in the shared global fit\&.
.RE
.SH "INPUT"
FILES
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.dat, \&.txt \- plain\-text experimental data
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.zip \- archive containing input data
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.sdf, \&.hdf5 \- Stelar data
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.sef \- Stelar field\-cycling data
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.sav \- fitteia/OneFit\-Engine description
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\&.json \- OneFit\-Engine description
.RE

The import options \-\-R1, \-\-sef\-R1\-file, \-\-range, \-\-gfilt, \-\-fit\-if, \-\-plot\-if, \-\-ist\-ffc\-Mz, and \-\-set\-err customize conversion of supported experimental formats; all of them apply only when building a definition from raw data (create and fit FUNCTION \&.\&.\&.), not when re\-fitting or re\-plotting a saved INPUT\-FILE\&.
.SH "COMMON"
OPTIONS

Each item below notes, in parentheses, which commands accept it: create, random, fit\-expr (fit FUNCTION \&.\&.\&.), fit\-file (fit INPUT\-FILE), and plot\&.
.SS Data import and model creation
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-dl, \-\-data\-label, \-\-data\-labels=TEXT \- supply labels and values used while importing data blocks\&. \fI(create, random; fit\-expr also has this option, but without the \-dl short alias)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-t, \-\-tags=TEXT \- assign data\-block tags\&. \fI(create, random, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-R1 \- import R1 rather than Mz data from supported IST\-FFC and Stelar files\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ist\-ffc\-Mz, \-\-ist\-ffc \- import Mz (rather than R1) data from an IST\-FFC file\&. \fI(create only)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-sf, \-\-sef\-R1\-file=FILE \- read frequencies from FILE while importing Stelar SEF data\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-r, \-\-range=TEXT \- select a range when importing Stelar data zones\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-gfilt=INTEGER \- apply a Gaussian smoothing filter during import\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-fi, \-\-fit\-if=CONDITION \- fit only data blocks whose tags satisfy CONDITION\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-pi, \-\-plot\-if=CONDITION \- plot only data blocks and fitted curves whose tags satisfy CONDITION\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-se, \-\-set\-err, \-\-err=EXPRESSION \- set or derive errors for ordinary data files\&. Supported expressions include a constant, a percentage, a multiplier, standard deviation, averaging, and splitting around a value \- for example 1\&.0, 1%, 10x, x10/100, std, std split at 5, or 10% avg split at 10\&.5\&. Does not apply to IST\-FFC, SEF, or HDF5 imports (their errors come from the instrument format itself)\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ac, \-\-aux\-code=SPECIFICATION \- add auxiliary C source and declarations\&. SPECIFICATION is a comma\-separated string whose first value is the C source filename and whose remaining values are declarations, for example \-\-aux\-code='functions\&.c, double custom(double x)' \&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.SS Fit control

These only apply once an actual MINUIT fit is performed, so \fInot\fR to create or plot\&.
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-fm, \-\-fit\-methods=METHODS \- whitespace\-separated MINUIT methods, run in order\&. Default: simp scan min minos\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr, fit\-file; random has no \-\-fit\-methods at all \- it reuses whatever the parsed function/definition already carries)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-g, \-\-global; \-i, \-\-individual; \-\-hybrid \- select the fitting mode (see FITTING MODES above for exact applicability)\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ro, \-\-remove\-outliers=SELECTION \- remove selected outliers, for example 2, 2\&.\&.5, or 1,3,5\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-rc, \-\-rchi2, \-\-reduced\-chi2 \- recalculate parameter errors for a chi\-square approximately equal to the number of degrees of freedom\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-eb, \-\-error\-bars, \-\-errorbars \- include error bars in fit output and plots\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-pco, \-\-peco, \-\-pearson\-correlation, \-\-R2 \- calculate the Pearson correlation quality coefficient\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-parallel, \-\-no\-parallel \- enable or disable parallel execution of hybrid/mixed fits (enabled by default)\&. Disabling it sets ONEFITE_NO_PARALLEL=1 for the process\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-workers=INTEGER \- set the worker count for mixed\-fit parallelism\&. Positive values set ONEFITE_WORKERS for the process\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ar, \-\-archive \- after a successful fit, append the exact command line to the local fit archive/log\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.SS Plot control
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-ax, \-\-autox; \-\-ay, \-\-autoy; \-\-axy, \-\-autoxy \- auto\-scale the x axis, y axis, or both\&. \fI(all commands)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-lx, \-\-logx, \-\-loglin; \-\-ly, \-\-logy, \-\-linlog; \-\-lxy, \-\-logxy, \-\-loglog \- logarithmic x, y, or both axes\&. \fI(all commands)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-n, \-\-Num, \-\-npts=INTEGER \- number of points in theoretical curves\&. Default: 100\&. \fI(create, random, plot; fit\-expr/fit\-file also accept \-\-num and \-N as extra aliases for the same option)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-SymbSize, \-\-ssz=NUMBER \- non\-negative plot\-symbol size\&. Default: 1\&.0\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-np, \-\-no\-plot \- run without producing plots\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file; random has the same option spelled \-\-inp/\-\-no\-plot instead; create never plots and plot always does, so neither has this flag)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-mp4, \-\-mpeg4 \- create All\&.mp4 from All\&.pdf via the installed pdf2mp4 helper\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.SS Output and workspace
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-o, \-\-st, \-\-save\-to=FILE \- save settings and fit results as a \&.json or \&.sav file\&. \fI(create, random, fit\-file \- \-\-to is an extra alias on these three; fit\-expr has the same option but without the \-\-to alias; plot has no \-\-save\-to)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-z, \-\-zt, \-\-zip\-to=FILE \- package the working result directory as FILE\&. \fI(random, fit\-expr, fit\-file \- on fit\-file it defaults to INPUT\-FILE's own basename; create never zips)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-pc, \-\-prco, \-\-print\-cols, \-\-print\-columns, \-\-cols=LIST \- select fit\-results columns by index or parameter name, after fitting\&. A suffix such as a+1 or a\-1 selects a column relative to parameter a\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-e, \-\-export \- when loading an engine file, export its data to data\-BASENAME\&.txt and any auxiliary source to AuxCode\-BASENAME\&.c\&. \fI(fit\-file only)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-wf, \-\-work\-folder=DIR \- parent of generated work directories\&. Default is the current directory, except for convert, which defaults to /tmp\&. \fI(all commands)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-\-rd, \-\-ram, \-\-ramdisk, \-\-RAMDisk, \-\-use\-ramdisk \- stage the work folder on a RAM disk instead of local disk\&. \fI(fit\-expr, fit\-file)\fR
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
\-q, \-\-quiet \- reduce informational log output; does not suppress the underlying result\&. \fI(create, random, fit\-expr, fit\-file; plot has no \-\-quiet)\fR
.RE
.SS Dynamic model overrides

Named options beginning with # update parts of the model expression (or a saved definition) before fitting\&. Quote these arguments to prevent shell comment and glob processing\&. \fI(create, fit\-expr, fit\-file; not available on random or plot)\fR

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b)=a+b*x' data\&.dat '\-\-#a=0\&.0[0<2]' '\-\-#x[0<10]'

.EE
.RE
.P
Option names not recognised as either a declared parameter/axis or one of the flags above print a warning ("\&.\&.\&.not defined\&.\&.\&.continue\&.\&.\&.") and are otherwise ignored, rather than aborting the run\&.
.SH "FILES"


Use onefite path to discover installation\-dependent paths\&. Important files include the installed C/META\-C\&.json, the installed aliases\&.json, an optional local \&./aliases\&.json, the service log (onefite path \-\-log), and the fit archive directory (onefite path \-\-archive)\&.
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"

.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
ONEFITE_NO_PARALLEL \- set to 1 internally by \-\-no\-parallel on onefite fit\&. Read by the compiled C fitting core to disable parallel (OpenMP) fitting of hybrid/mixed data blocks\&.
.RE
.RS 2n
.IP \(bu 2m
ONEFITE_WORKERS \- set internally by a positive \-\-workers=N on onefite fit\&. Read by the same C fitting core to cap the number of parallel fitting workers used for hybrid/mixed fits\&.
.RE
.SH "EXIT"
STATUS

The command returns zero after successful completion\&. Invalid input, missing files or aliases, generated\-code compilation errors, and fitting errors return a nonzero status\&. Some administrative commands delegate their status to external programs (git, systemctl, zef, \&.\&.\&.)\&.
.SH "SECURITY"


start\-web\-engine accepts uploaded model and data files and compiles and executes the resulting generated C code\&. Bind it to 127\&.0\&.0\&.1 unless remote access is deliberately required and protected by appropriate firewall and access controls\&.

upgrade, uninstall, and systemd service management invoke git, installation scripts, and other external commands, and in some modes sudo\&. Review their effects before using them on production systems\&.

Fit, plot, service, and RAM\-disk operations remove and recreate working directories (rm \-fr the target folder before writing to it)\&. Do not point \-\-work\-folder at a directory containing unrelated files under a name that a generated result would reuse\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"

.SS Fit a straight line

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a:0,b:1)=a+b*x' data\&.dat

.EE
.RE
.SS Use bounded and fixed parameters

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y[0<10](x[0<5],a:1[0<10],b=2)=a+b*x' data\&.dat

.EE
.RE
.SS Save results and create an archive

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit '#1exp' data\&.txt \-\-save\-to=fit\&.json \-\-zip\-to=fit\&.zip \-\-archive

.EE
.RE
.SS Refit an existing description

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit fit\&.json \-\-fit\-methods='simp scan min' \-\-autoxy

.EE
.RE
.SS Run a global or hybrid fit

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b)=a+b*x' sample\-*\&.dat \-\-global \-\-workers=2
onefite fit '#2exp' sample\&.hdf5 \-\-hybrid \-\-workers=2

.EE
.RE
.SS Set errors and remove outliers

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b)=a+b*x' data\&.dat \
    \-\-set\-err='10% avg split at 10\&.5' \-\-remove\-outliers='1,3,5'

.EE
.RE
.SS Select result columns

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite fit 'y(x,a,b)=a+b*x' data\&.dat \-\-print\-columns='2,a,a+1'

.EE
.RE
.SS Create a definition once, fit it later

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite create 'y(x,a,b) = a + b*x' data\&.dat \-\-save\-to=fit\-def\&.json
onefite fit fit\-def\&.json \-\-export
onefite fit fit\-def\&.json \-\-individual \-\-fit\-methods='simp scan min'

.EE
.RE
.SS Inspect a model and installed paths

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite list models
onefite help BPP
onefite path \-\-aliases

.EE
.RE
.SS Start a local\-only HTTP service

.RS 4m
.EX
onefite service start \-\-ip=127\&.0\&.0\&.1 \-\-port=8142

.EE
.RE
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"

.P
If an alias is not found, onefite prints the installed and local alias locations and the available keys\&. Use onefite list aliases to inspect them\&.

If generated C code fails to compile, inspect compile\&.log in the generated work directory\&. For undeclared helper functions, provide their implementation and declarations with \-\-aux\-code\&.

If service startup fails, inspect onefite service log, verify the bind address exists, and check whether the port is already in use or blocked by a firewall\&.
.SH "SEE"
ALSO

onefite \-\-help, onefite man, onefite list models, onefite help MODEL, https://github\&.com/fitteia/OneFit\-Engine
